    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Two friends (say ’A’ and ’B’) could not decide whether to play a racing game or a\nboxing game on Xbox. They decide to play a card-game first. If ’A’ wins at least x\nrounds out of the y rounds of the card game played, then the boxing game will be\nplayed. The chances of ’A’ winning in any round of the card game is a : b. Find the\nprobability that the boxing game will be played on Xbox? \nHint: If the chances of happening of an event is x : y then, the probability equals\nx\nx + y"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "sum(i=x..y,binom(y,i)*(a/(a+b))^i*(b/(a+b))^(y-i))",
        "sum(i=x..y,binom(y,i)(a/(a+b))^i(b/(a+b))^(y-i))",
        "sum(i=x..y,binom(y,i)*(a/(a+b))**i*(b/(a+b))**(y-i))"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "The number of rounds won by A is Binomial(y,a/(a+b)); sum its mass function from x wins through y wins."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Let X ∼ Binomial(n, p). If the probabilities of x and x + 1 successes are a and, b\nrespectively, then find the parameter ’p’ of the distribution."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "b*(x+1)/(a*(n-x)+b*(x+1))",
        "b(x+1)/(a(n-x)+b(x+1))"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Divide the Binomial probability at x+1 by the probability at x, set the ratio to b/a, and solve for p."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "If the expected number of sixes hit by a batsman on n balls is e and the variance for the\nsame is v, then what is the probability of him hitting at least one six on any randomly\nselected n balls?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "1-(v/e)^n",
        "1-(v/e)**n"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Binomial mean np=e and variance np(1−p)=v imply 1−p=v/e. Subtract the probability of no sixes from one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "The probability of a student clearing a competitive exam is 1\nm. If he gives the exam\nn times, then what is the probability of him clearing the exam at least twice?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "1-(1-1/m)^n-(n/m)*(1-1/m)^(n-1)",
        "1-(1-1/m)^n-(n/m)(1-1/m)^(n-1)",
        "1-(1-1/m)**n-(n/m)*(1-1/m)**(n-1)"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "For Binomial(n,1/m), subtract the probabilities of zero and one successes from one."
        }
      ]
    },
